+The NightSky HD image and shooting stars get another six stops (64×) after this conversion. The
+catalogue and Gaia retain their physical scale. The Night brightness and Starlight controls still
+apply to both sources. At solar contact the host integrates the uncovered limb-darkened photosphere
+and applies the totality floor to the sunlight entering NUMOS. Its sky and cloud bakes and emitted
+distant Sun therefore share one eclipse. The visible part of the Sun and its corona keep their
+unocculted surface radiance behind the lunar mask. At high-Sun totality the host reveals real stars
+using the transmitted daylight and draws their full field, since the daytime LUT contains no blurred
+starlight to subtract.
+
 ### Lights
 
 The sun, moons and lightning are externally tracked lights, one frame behind the renderer. Distant lights with `lightFlagCloudShadowed` get the cloud shadow in direct and indirect next event estimation, and in the volume integration. Resampling ignores the shadow.
